A||N||5||jaguiler||Painting the Fiero - Question - Honest answers please...||||1||
Z||000000||jaguiler||04-09-2001||10:21 PM||||Hi all, earlier today I posted the same subject but more specific to Maryland people.  Now I would like to ask all of you...  I have limited funds but my GT needs a paint job.  I used to have a Jeep CJ7 which Earl Schieb painted for me.  It seemed like pretty good paint.  Very affordable too....  <BR>What do you guys think of Earl Schieb?  Quality? Has anyone had their Fiero painted there?  Any opinions?  I would like to have my car painted but I would like to keep it around $500 - $1000 max......<P>Thank you all,<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||04-10-2001||12:01 AM||||I had my '69 Firebird painted at Earl Scheib when I was in High School.  I did all the prep work myself and the job was definately worth the $100 I spent, but that's the rub.  I got a good value for my money, but we are talking about a $100 paint job here.  It looked good from 20' away, but up close you could see the overspray, orange peel, etc.  They even got some overspray on my interior door panels!  At least it cleaned off.  Also, their paint is very low quality.  After a few years, the bright red looked more like a powdery pink.  The pinstrips fell off the car and took the paint with them!  Overall, it's worth the money, but you are talking bargain basement.  It's only one step up from using spray cans in the driveway.  Heck, you can't even buy enough quality paint to paint your car for what Scheib charges for the whole deal.  That should tell you something.  Other than painting it yourself, you might try Maaco, if you can find one.  Anywhere else will probably blow your $500-1K budget.  For under $1K, you could buy the equipment, good paint, and do it yourself with money left over.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||04-10-2001||12:10 AM||||Friend of mine had them paint his 67 Impala.  Let's just say better him than me.  It was extremely disappointing.  I'll never take a car there, even a bad looking one.  They shouldn't be in that business if they can't do a better job than that.  They're ripping people off, IMO.  I'd say stay far away from there.<P>Editing cause I just remembered that one of our members and fellow Houstonian told me he got one of their paint jobs on his Fiero and within a few months it needed painting again.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000003||jaguiler||04-10-2001||09:58 AM||||OK.... that you for your opions... I will probably wait a little longer.. and wait to take it to another place.... prob go price shopping... we have a few rural places around here taht some people say do a good job at a better price... I figure that it is a small car...can't be that much..... oh well... time to bite the bullet.... <P>I will also inquire about getting just my rear deck painted and the wing.  In reality it is the only thing that needs painting... I may save some money if I do that....<BR><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||146.145.42.98||reg||1
Z||000004||fierolarry||04-10-2001||12:24 PM||||I had the wing and trunk lid on my 87 GT painted last year.Paint was badly faded.I got their 2 stage paint job.Cost me $195.00  I had to take it back twice to get it wet sanded to take out runs in spoiler & dust particles in paint.Scheib shop by me Has dust problem. There was no overspray problem and it looks very good.You have to keep after them and tellm them you wont accept a lousy job. I also had them paint my 68 Mustang Fastback 2 years ago. Did a great job masking w/ very little overspray. but needed to get car wetsanded because of dust particles in paint job. The price for fiero included paint match from local Sherwin Williams paint store. They do auto paint!<BR>Also you dont get their cheepo paint job. You get their top Level 3 paint job with a separate clear coat applied. I've had no problem with any peeling or fading on my 68 mustang that was done 2 years ago. If you want to talk about their work more please E-mail me<BR>[This message has been edited by fierolarry (edited 04-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierolarry (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-10-2001||01:09 PM||||MAACO will do a better job than Shieb for a little more money. They all use cheaper paint that dont hold up as well. PREP IS 90% of the job, do your own sanding, part removing and as much masking as you can yourself. After all if the guys spraying 10-20 cars a day. at least he does know by now how to spray decently.||||reg||1
